# See backend/.dockerignore for the full rationale. Same two problems:
# `COPY . .` ran after `npm ci` and clobbered the container's node_modules with
# the Windows host's, and it copied .env files into the build stage.
#
# The frontend leak is narrower than the backend's — Vite only exposes
# VITE_-prefixed vars to client code, and vite.config.ts discards its loadEnv()
# result — but frontend/.env.local defines VITE_AZURE_VOICELIVE_API_KEY, which
# WOULD be inlined into the bundle the moment any code referenced it. Keep the
# env files out of the image entirely so that mistake cannot happen.
node_modules
npm-debug.log

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

dist
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile

# Pre-migration Gemini snapshots; excluded from tsconfig and never imported.
legacy

*.log
